- **`Verse(n)`** returns an error for `n` outside 0–99. It handles the special cases for 0 bottles ("No more bottles… Go to the store"), 1 bottle ("Take it down…", singular "bottle") and 2 bottles (next line says "1 bottle"). Every other verse uses the general form. Each verse ends with a newline.
- **`Verses(start, stop)`** returns an error if either bound is outside 0–99 or if `start < stop`. Otherwise it joins the verses from `start` down to `stop`, with a blank line between them.
