I'll implement a doubly linked list with raw pointers (`NonNull`), a cursor, an iterator, `Drop`, and manual `Send`/`Sync` implementations.

Design notes:
- `LinkedList<T>` holds `front`, `back` (`Option<NonNull<Node<T>>>`), and `len`, plus a `PhantomData<Box<Node<T>>>` for ownership/covariance.
- `Cursor` holds a mutable reference to the list and a `current` node pointer. When the list is empty, `current` is `None`.
- `take` removes the current element and moves to the neighbor closest to the back (next if it exists, else prev).
- `insert_after`/`insert_before` work on an empty list (the new element becomes the current one).
- The `pre_implemented` module (not shown) uses the cursor methods, so I keep the cursor semantics as described.

