- **`Verse(n)`** returns one verse, ending with a newline. It returns an error if `n` is outside 0–99. Verse 0 is the "Go to the store" verse, and verse 1 says "Take it down" with the singular "bottle".
- **`Verses(start, stop)`** returns the verses from `start` down to `stop`, inclusive. They are separated by a blank line and the text ends with a single newline. It returns an error if either number is outside 0–99 or if `start < stop`.
