I implemented `PythagoreanTriplet` with a working builder, and added `equals`, `hashCode` and `toString` so triplets can be compared and printed.

- **`thatSumTo(sum)`:** Combining `a + b + c = N` with `a² + b² = c²` gives `b = N(N − 2a) / (2(N − a))`. So the code loops over `a` and checks whether `b` comes out as a whole number, rather than looping over both `a` and `b`. It then keeps only triplets with `a < b < c`.
- **`withFactorsLessThanOrEqualTo(maxFactor)`:** The largest side `c` must be at most `maxFactor`. If no sum was given, the code searches all `a < b` up to `maxFactor` and checks whether `a² + b²` is a perfect square.
- **Both set:** The sum-based search runs first, then results are filtered by `maxFactor`.
- **Neither set:** `build()` throws an `IllegalStateException`, because the result would be unbounded.

PythagoreanTriplet.java
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

class PythagoreanTriplet {

    private final int a;
    private final int b;
    private final int c;

    PythagoreanTriplet(int a, int b, int c) {
        this.a = a;
        this.b = b;
        this.c = c;
    }

    static TripletListBuilder makeTripletsList() {
        return new TripletListBuilder();
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) {
            return true;
        }
        if (o == null || getClass() != o.getClass()) {
            return false;
        }
        PythagoreanTriplet other = (PythagoreanTriplet) o;
        return a == other.a && b == other.b && c == other.c;
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        int result = a;
        result = 31 * result + b;
        result = 31 * result + c;
        return result;
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return "{" + a + ", " + b + ", " + c + "}";
    }

    static class TripletListBuilder {

        private Integer sum = null;
        private Integer maxFactor = null;

        TripletListBuilder thatSumTo(int sum) {
            this.sum = sum;
            return this;
        }

        TripletListBuilder withFactorsLessThanOrEqualTo(int maxFactor) {
            this.maxFactor = maxFactor;
            return this;
        }

        List<PythagoreanTriplet> build() {
            if (sum == null && maxFactor == null) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Either a sum or a maximum factor must be specified.");
            }

            List<PythagoreanTriplet> result = new ArrayList<>();

            if (sum != null) {
                buildForSum(result);
            } else {
                buildForMaxFactor(result);
            }

            return result;
        }

        private void buildForSum(List<PythagoreanTriplet> result) {
            long n = sum;
            if (n <= 0) {
                return;
            }
            for (long a = 1; a * 3 < n; a++) {
                long numerator = n * (n - 2 * a);
                long denominator = 2 * (n - a);
                if (denominator <= 0 || numerator % denominator != 0) {
                    continue;
                }
                long b = numerator / denominator;
                long c = n - a - b;
                if (a < b && b < c && a * a + b * b == c * c) {
                    if (maxFactor == null || c <= maxFactor) {
                        result.add(new PythagoreanTriplet((int) a, (int) b, (int) c));
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        private void buildForMaxFactor(List<PythagoreanTriplet> result) {
            long max = maxFactor;
            for (long a = 1; a <= max; a++) {
                for (long b = a + 1; b <= max; b++) {
                    long cSquared = a * a + b * b;
                    long c = (long) Math.sqrt((double) cSquared);
                    while (c * c < cSquared) {
                        c++;
                    }
                    while (c * c > cSquared) {
                        c--;
                    }
                    if (c * c == cSquared && c > b && c <= max) {
                        result.add(new PythagoreanTriplet((int) a, (int) b, (int) c));
                    }
                }
            }
        }

    }

}
